36. Article 226 of the Criminal Law is amended to read: "A person who, by means of violence or threat, commits any of the following acts, if the circumstances are serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention, and/or a fine; if the circumstances are especially serious, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years and a fine:
"(1) forcing another person to buy or sell goods;
"(2) forcing another person to provide or accept services;
"(3) forcing another person to participate in or withdraw from bidding or auction;
"(4) forcing another person to transfer or acquire shares, bonds, or other assets of a company or enterprise; or
"(5) forcing another person to participate in or withdraw from specific business operations."

42. Article 293 of the Criminal Law is amended to read: "A person who commits any of the following acts of picking quarrels and provoking troubles, thereby disrupting social order, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years, criminal detention, or public surveillance:
"(1) beating another person at will, if the circumstances are egregious;
"(2) chasing, intercepting, verbally abusing, or intimidating another person, if the circumstances are egregious;
"(3) forcibly taking or demanding, or arbitrarily damaging or occupying, public or private property, if the circumstances are serious; or
"(4) creating a disturbance in a public place, thereby causing serious disorder in the public place.
"A person who gathers others to repeatedly commit the acts in the preceding paragraph, thereby seriously disrupting social order, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than 10 years, and may also be fined."

45. Paragraph 1 of Article 328 of the Criminal Law is amended to read: "A person who excavates and robs a site of ancient culture or an ancient tomb of historical, artistic, or scientific value shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than 10 years and a fine; if the circumstances are relatively minor, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years, criminal detention, or public surveillance, and a fine; if any of the following circumstances exist, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than 10 years or life imprisonment, and a fine or confiscation of property:
"(1) excavating and robbing a site of ancient culture or an ancient tomb designated as a major cultural relic protection unit under State protection or a cultural relic protection unit at the provincial level;
"(2) being the ringleader of a group that excavates and robs sites of ancient culture or ancient tombs;
"(3) repeatedly excavating and robbing sites of ancient culture or ancient tombs; or
"(4) excavating and robbing a site of ancient culture or an ancient tomb and stealing valuable cultural relics or causing serious damage to valuable cultural relics."
